adjudication.rationale:
In `checkIfIsAvailable`, the new “within normal work hours” check computes both `start` and `end` from `slotStartTime`:
```ts
const start = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
const end = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
```
This makes `end` equal to the slot start, so `end > workingHour.endTime` will never detect slots whose *end* time exceeds `workingHour.endTime` (it should be based on `slotEndTime`). As a result, longer slots that start before the end of working hours but run past it can be incorrectly treated as available.
